==Strategy==
The less Wave Attacks the Crazed Titan performs, the better; if it does manage to fire off a Wave, it will cripple most, if not all the units on the field. If the player gets lucky and the Crazed Titan didn't create many Waves, stalling it isn't actually that hard due to its sluggish foreswing as long as the peons don't push too badly.

Units that have [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] and [[Wave Shield|Wave Blocker]] can help greatly relieve the potential RNG of this stage, allowing the player to stand their ground easier in case the Crazed Titan manages to Wave multiple times.

